# Schnapsen Project Conventions

## Crate Structure

- **schnapsen-model**: Pure data structures. No I/O, minimal dependencies. Types: `Card`, `Suit`, `Rank`, `GameState`, `GameType`, `Player`, `Trick`.
- **schnapsen-engine**: Game logic (validation, apply_move, AI). Depends on schnapsen-model.
- **schnapsen-cli**: TUI using ratatui. Depends on model + engine.

## Game Types

Game types from German rules use `GameType` enum. Card order varies per game:
- Normal/Bauernschnapser: Ass > Zehner > König > Ober > Unter
- Assenbettler/Zehnergang: Ass lowest
- Königsgang: Zehner lowest
- Damengang: König lowest

Use `Rank::order_in_game(game_type)` for comparisons.

## Card and Move Validation

- Use `schnapsen_engine::get_valid_moves(state)` to get legal plays
- `apply_move` enforces Farbzwang (follow suit) and Stichzwang (trump when can't follow)

## Testing

- Unit tests in each crate under `#[cfg(test)] mod tests`
- Model tests: card ordering, trick scoring, deal distribution
- Engine tests: valid move generation

## Naming

- German game terms in docs (Rufer, Talon, Stich, etc.)
- Rust identifiers use PascalCase for types, snake_case for functions
